-take-on-iowa-state-on-first-stop-of-road-swing</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/volleyball-mountaineers-take-on-iowa-state-on-first-stop-of-road-swing</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball team huddles before a point against Arizona" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/DAK01986.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (11-8, 4-5 Big 12) travels to Ames, Iowa, to take on Iowa State at Hilton Coliseum. First serve is set for 7:30 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/DAK01986.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/DAK01986.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball team huddles before a point against Arizona</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/DAK01986.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:52:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59611</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU Olympic Sports Coaches Show Lineup For November</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/general-wvu-olympic-sports-coaches-show-lineup-for-november</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/general-wvu-olympic-sports-coaches-show-lineup-for-november</guid><category>General, Men's Swimming &amp; Diving, Rifle, Women's Swimming &amp; Diving, Wrestling</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The WVU Olympic Sports Coaches Show will have three episodes in November 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/2026-27_Olympic_Sport_Coaches_Show-Nov.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The Mountaineer Sports Network from Learfield has announced the November schedule for its popular WVU Olympic Sports Coaches Show live from the Mountain State Brewing Company in Morgantown.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/2026-27_Olympic_Sport_Coaches_Show-Nov.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/2026-27_Olympic_Sport_Coaches_Show-Nov.jpg"><media:title>The WVU Olympic Sports Coaches Show will have three episodes in November 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/2026-27_Olympic_Sport_Coaches_Show-Nov.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:30:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>3</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59607</s:story_id></item><item><title>Forbes Named to Katrina McClain Award Watch List</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/womens-basketball-forbes-named-to-katrina-mcclain-award-watch-list</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/womens-basketball-forbes-named-to-katrina-mcclain-award-watch-list</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Skylar Forbes takes part in a preseason practice ahead of the 2026-27 season" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/GB706710.jpg" /><br /><br />SPRINGFIELD, MASS. — The Naismith Basketball Hall of Fame announced the 20 watch-list candidates for the 2027 Karl Malone Award and, in partnership with the Women's Basketball Coaches Association (WBCA), the 20 watch-list candidates for the 2027 Katrina McClain Award. The annual Karl Malone Award, named after the Class of 2010 Hall of Famer and two-time NBA Most Valuable Player, celebrates its 13th year by recognizing the top power forward in NCAA Division I men's college basketball. The Katrina McClain Award, now in its 10th year, recognizes the top power forward in NCAA Division I women's college basketball. It is named after the two-time All-American, 1987 National Player of the Year, and Class of 2012 Hall of Famer.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/GB706710.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/GB706710.jpg"><media:title>Skylar Forbes takes part in a preseason practice ahead of the 2026-27 season</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/GB706710.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59605</s:story_id></item></channel></rss>